---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Methodology | HUMANITY" description="How HUMANITY discovers, verifies, and publishes human events. Full transparency on sources, algorithms, and editorial standards.">
  <div class="min-h-screen">
    <header class="border-b border-humanity-border bg-humanity-darker/80 backdrop-blur-sm sticky top-0 z-50">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between h-16">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <svg class="w-8 h-8 text-humanity-accent" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
                <path d="M2 12h20" />
                <path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z" />
              </svg>
              <span class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-humanity-text">HUMANITY</span>
            </a>
            <span class="text-humanity-textMuted">/</span>
            <span class="text-humanity-text">Methodology</span>
          </div>
          <nav class="hidden md:flex items-center gap-6">
            <a href="/" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Home</a>
            <a href="/map" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Map</a>
            <a href="/events" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Live Events</a>
            <a href="/protests" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Protests</a>
            <a href="/conflicts" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Conflicts</a>
            <a href="/human-cost" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Human Cost</a>
            <a href="/countries" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Countries</a>
            <a href="/timelines" class="text-humanity-textMuted hover:text-humanity-text transition-colors text-sm font-medium">Timelines</a>
            <a href="/methodology" class="text-humanity-accent font-medium text-sm">Methodology</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 space-y-16">
      <header class="text-center">
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-4">Methodology</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-humanity-textMuted max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          How we discover, verify, structure, and publish human events. Full transparency on every step.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Core Principles -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #7c3aed;">🎯</span>
          Core Principles
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-violet-500">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-2">The Event is the Central Object</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted">An article is only a presentation layer around an event. The event itself—structured, sourced, versioned—is the primary data entity.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-emerald-500">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-2">No Number Without Provenance</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted">Every figure—deaths, injuries, participants, displaced—must trace to one or more source records. We never store a number without its evidence chain.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-amber-500">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-2">AI is a Tool, Not a Source</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted">AI-generated statements are never evidence. AI assists with classification, extraction, clustering, and synthesis—but never invents facts or fills missing numbers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-blue-500">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-2">Traceable Claims</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted">Every factual claim links to a source quote, a source URL, and a confidence assessment. You can always verify what we say.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-red-500">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-2">Uncertainty Over False Precision</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted">We distinguish: reported, verified, corroborated, disputed, estimated, unknown. We never turn uncertain information into false precision.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Source Acquisition -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #3b82f6;">📡</span>
          Source Acquisition
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Layer 1: Broad Discovery (GDELT)</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mb-4">We use the Global Database of Events, Language, and Tone (GDELT) for global, multilingual news discovery across 65+ languages. GDELT provides structured event records, article URLs, and metadata for initial candidate detection.</p>
            <div class="card p-4 bg-humanity-darker/50">
              <p class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted"><strong>Why GDELT:</strong> Unparalleled global coverage, structured output, free access. <strong>Limitations:</strong> Noisy, requires heavy filtering, not a verified source itself.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Layer 2: Structured Datasets</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-humanity-textMuted">
              <li><strong>UCDP (Uppsala Conflict Data Program):</strong> Authoritative conflict event data, battle-related deaths</li>
              <li><strong>ReliefWeb / UN OCHA:</strong> Humanitarian reports, displacement figures, disaster data</li>
              <li><strong>ACLED:</strong> Armed Conflict Location & Event Data (when available)</li>
              <li><strong>UNHCR / IOM:</strong> Official displacement and refugee statistics</li>
              <li><strong>WHO:</strong> Health emergency and disease outbreak data</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Layer 3: RSS & Official Feeds</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mb-4">Configurable source registry (<code>sources.yaml</code>) with global/regional news, government feeds, NGO reports, and UN agencies. Each source has priority, poll interval, and robots.txt compliance.</p>
            <div class="card p-4 bg-humanity-darker/50">
              <p class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted"><strong>Principle:</strong> Respect robots.txt, rate limits, copyright. Prefer RSS and public APIs. Never scrape indiscriminately. Store metadata and link to original.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Discovery & Processing Pipeline -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #f97316;">⚙️</span>
          Discovery & Processing Pipeline
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Automated Pipeline Stages</h3>
            <ol class="space-y-3 text-humanity-textMuted">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">1.</span><strong>DISCOVER</strong> – Fetch from GDELT, RSS, datasets</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">2.</span><strong>FETCH METADATA</strong> – Title, URL, date, source</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">3.</span><strong>NORMALIZE URL</strong> – Canonicalize, deduplicate</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">4.</span><strong>DEDUPLICATE</strong> – Exact URL, content hash, title similarity</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">5.</span><strong>EXTRACT CANDIDATE FACTS</strong> – LLM-structured extraction (Gemini)</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">6.</span><strong>CLASSIFY EVENT</strong> – Type, location, date, severity</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">7.</span><strong>CLUSTER RELATED ARTICLES</strong> – Multi-source → single event</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">8.</span><strong>CREATE EVENT CANDIDATE</strong> – Structured event with claims</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">9.</span><strong>VERIFY & SCORE</strong> – Cross-source corroboration, importance scoring</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">10.</span><strong>PUBLISH DECISION</strong> – Auto-publish / Auto-publish with warning / Hold</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-humanity-accent font-bold">11.</span><strong>GENERATE</strong> – Event page, map marker, summary, share card</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Event Clustering -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #10b981;">🔗</span>
          Event Clustering (Multi-Source → Single Event)
        </h2>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mb-4">Ten news articles describing one protest become ONE event with multiple sources.</p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded" style="background: #141414;">
              <h4 class="font-medium text-humanity-text mb-2">Clustering Signals</h4>
              <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
                <li>✓ Exact URL canonicalization</li>
                <li>✓ Title similarity (fuzzy matching)</li>
                <li>✓ Named entity overlap (actors, organizations)</li>
                <li>✓ Location proximity (within 50km)</li>
                <li>✓ Temporal proximity (within 48 hours)</li>
                <li>✓ Semantic similarity (embeddings)</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded" style="background: #141414;">
              <h4 class="font-medium text-humanity-text mb-2">Example Cluster</h4>
              <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
                <li>Reuters: "Protests in Paris over pension reform"</li>
                <li>AP: "French unions mobilize against retirement age"</li>
                <li>Le Monde: "Manifestations à Paris : 15 000 selon la CGT"</li>
                <li>Gov statement: "Ministry confirms 7 arrests"</li>
                <li>GDELT: Event code 1401, Paris, 2026-10-08</li>
                <li><strong>→ ONE EVENT with 5 sources</strong></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- AI Role & Constraints -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #ef4444;">🤖</span>
          AI Role & Constraints
        </h2>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-3 text-green-400">AI Performs</h3>
              <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
                <li>✓ Event classification</li>
                <li>✓ Entity extraction (actors, locations, dates)</li>
                <li>✓ Fact/claim extraction with quotes</li>
                <li>✓ Event clustering assistance</li>
                <li>✓ Importance & novelty scoring</li>
                <li>✓ Source comparison & conflict detection</li>
                <li>✓ Summary & headline generation</li>
                <li>✓ Daily brief & social card copy</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-3 text-red-400">AI Must NOT</h3>
              <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
                <li>✗ Invent facts or casualty figures</li>
                <li>✗ Fill missing numbers</li>
                <li>✗ Pretend verification</li>
                <li>✗ Merge incompatible numbers</li>
                <li>✗ Create fake citations</li>
                <li>✗ Publish unsourced claims</li>
                <li>✗ Generate content without structured output</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 p-4 rounded" style="background: #2d1515; border: 1px solid #ef444440;">
            <h4 class="font-medium text-humanity-text mb-2">Structured Output Only</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">We never ask for free-form prose. We request JSON with strict schema validation (Pydantic). Malformed output is rejected and retried.</p>
            <pre class="mt-3 p-3 rounded text-xs overflow-x-auto" style="background: #050505;"><code>&#123;"event_type": "PROTEST", "claims": [&#123;"type": "participants", "min": 10000, "max": 20000, "source_id": "..."&#125;], "confidence_score": 82&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Scoring & Publishing Policy -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #f97316;">📊</span>
          Scoring & Publishing Policy
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Interestingness Engine (Event Score)</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mb-4">Weighted formula (configurable in <code>scoring.yaml</code>):</p>
            <pre class="p-4 rounded text-sm overflow-x-auto" style="background: #050505;"><code>score =
  0.25 × importance
+ 0.20 × human_impact
+ 0.15 × novelty
+ 0.15 × corroboration
+ 0.10 × velocity
+ 0.10 × public_interest
+ 0.05 × unusualness
− penalties (duplicate, low confidence, single source, old event)</code></pre>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Three-Tier Publishing</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="p-4 rounded border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5">
                <h4 class="font-medium text-emerald-400 mb-2">✅ AUTO-PUBLISH</h4>
                <ul class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted space-y-1">
                  <li>High confidence</li>
                  <li>Multiple independent sources</li>
                  <li>Clear location & date</li>
                  <li>No major contradictions</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 rounded border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/5">
                <h4 class="font-medium text-amber-400 mb-2">⚠️ AUTO-PUBLISH WITH WARNING</h4>
                <ul class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted space-y-1">
                  <li>Sources disagree on numbers</li>
                  <li>Early/developing reports</li>
                  <li>Page clearly states: "Reports differ"</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 rounded border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
                <h4 class="font-medium text-red-400 mb-2">🔴 HOLD</h4>
                <ul class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted space-y-1">
                  <li>Single weak source</li>
                  <li>Location/date uncertain</li>
                  <li>Major contradictions</li>
                  <li>Possible misinformation</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Human Cost Metrics -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #ef4444;">💔</span>
          Human Cost Metrics
        </h2>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mb-4">We never combine incompatible datasets. Each metric specifies exactly what is counted, by whom, and when.</p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded" style="background: #141414;">
              <h4 class="font-medium text-humanity-text mb-2">Supported Metric Types</h4>
              <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
                <li>reported_deaths</li>
                <li>reported_injuries</li>
                <li>civilian_deaths</li>
                <li>combatant_deaths</li>
                <li>displaced_people</li>
                <li>reported_airstrikes</li>
                <li>reported_attacks</li>
                <li>reported_missiles</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded" style="background: #141414;">
              <h4 class="font-medium text-humanity-text mb-2">Every Metric Includes</h4>
              <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
                <li>value + unit</li>
                <li>source + source date</li>
                <li>methodology</li>
                <li>confidence level</li>
                <li>cumulative vs period-specific</li>
                <li>geography scope</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Revision & Contradiction Handling -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #0ea5e9;">🔄</span>
          Revision & Contradiction Handling
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-3">Event Revisions</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mb-4">Events evolve. We store historical claims, never overwrite.</p>
            <div class="p-4 rounded" style="background: #141414; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.875rem;">
              <code>10:00 → Report: 5 killed (Source A)</code><br>
              <code>12:00 → Official: 8 killed (Source B)</code><br>
              <code>15:00 → UN: 7 killed (Source C)</code><br><br>
              <code>UI shows: "Earlier reports: 5 (A), 8 (B). Latest: 7 (UN)."</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-3">Contradiction Engine</h3>
            <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mb-4">Detects conflicting reports and flags them explicitly.</p>
            <div class="p-4 rounded" style="background: #141414;">
              <p class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted"><strong>Source A:</strong> 23 deaths (UN)</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted"><strong>Source B:</strong> 21 deaths (Gov)</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted"><strong>System:</strong> value_min=21, value_max=23, status=conflicting_reports</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Tech Stack -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #888;">🛠️</span>
          Technology Stack
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Backend (Python)</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
              <li><strong>httpx</strong> – Async HTTP client</li>
              <li><strong>feedparser</strong> – RSS/Atom parsing</li>
              <li><strong>BeautifulSoup</strong> – HTML parsing</li>
              <li><strong>Pydantic</strong> – Data validation</li>
              <li><strong>RapidFuzz</strong> – String similarity</li>
              <li><strong>Google Generative AI</strong> – Gemini API</li>
              <li><strong>Tavily</strong> – Search API (optional)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Frontend (Astro)</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
              <li><strong>Astro</strong> – Static site generation</li>
              <li><strong>MapLibre GL JS</strong> – Interactive maps</li>
              <li><strong>Tailwind CSS</strong> – Styling</li>
              <li><strong>ECharts</strong> – Visualizations</li>
              <li><strong>TypeScript</strong> – Type safety</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Deployment (Free Tier)</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
              <li><strong>GitHub Actions</strong> – Scheduled ingestion</li>
              <li><strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> – Static hosting</li>
              <li><strong>Cloudflare D1</strong> – Database (later)</li>
              <li><strong>GitHub Secrets</strong> – API keys</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Data Storage (MVP)</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
              <li><strong>Local JSON</strong> – Events, sources, claims</li>
              <li><strong>Generated JSON</strong> – Map, timeline, stats</li>
              <li><strong>Static files</strong> – Event pages, briefs</li>
              <li>→ Migrate to D1 when JSON becomes cumbersome</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Schedule & Budget -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #888;">⏰</span>
          Schedule & Resource Budget
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Autonomous Schedule</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
              <li><strong>Every 30 min:</strong> Discovery, processing, publishing</li>
              <li><strong>Every 2–4 hrs:</strong> Recheck developing stories, update casualties</li>
              <li><strong>Every 6 hrs:</strong> Rebuild daily summaries, refresh rankings</li>
              <li><strong>Daily:</strong> Historical aggregation, sitemap, cleanup</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-humanity-text mb-4">Economic Model (Free Tier)</h3>
            <div class="p-4 rounded" style="background: #141414; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.875rem;">
              <code>1000 discovered articles</code><br>
              <code>→ 200 candidates (deterministic filter)</code><br>
              <code>→ 50 meaningful events (clustering)</code><br>
              <code>→ 20 verified (LLM extraction)</code><br>
              <code>→ 5–15 published</code>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-humanity-textMuted mt-3">Gemini: 80% extraction, 15% verification, 5% editorial. Tavily: only high-interest cases.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What We Don't Do -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span style="color: #ef4444;">🚫</span>
          What We Don't Do (Yet)
        </h2>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-humanity-textMuted">
            <li>No chatbot, no mobile app, no user accounts</li>
            <li>No comments, no social network, no subscriptions</li>
            <li>No AI-generated images or videos</li>
            <li>No full-text news republishing (copyright)</li>
            <li>No paid APIs, paid scraping, paid LLMs (unless required later)</li>
            <li>No browser extensions, no premium features</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-humanity-textMuted mt-4"><strong>Focus:</strong> Prove that autonomous event discovery + verification + visualization + SEO + publication creates useful traffic.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Footer CTA -->
      <section class="text-center pt-8 border-t border-humanity-border">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-humanity-text mb-4">Open Source & Transparent</h2>
